1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:31,886 --> 00:00:33,847
The clumsy kiss…

3
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:35,014
Forget it.

4
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:40,562
This one's for real.

5
00:00:49,279 --> 00:00:54,033
I don't get why people say that even rags
can look designer on a great body.

6
00:00:54,701 --> 00:00:57,704
It takes hard work to get a great body.

7
00:00:57,787 --> 00:00:59,205
Why dress yourself in rags?

8
00:01:13,178 --> 00:01:14,470
DETECTIVE AGENCY

9
00:01:15,138 --> 00:01:17,390
-Yes?
-We found a patient named Go Ji-won.

10
00:01:17,473 --> 00:01:20,018
In her early thirties.
Admitted two weeks ago.

11
00:01:20,101 --> 00:01:22,061
She's at a university hospital
in Gyeongbuk.

12
00:01:22,145 --> 00:01:24,189
Are you sure the patient is Go Ji-won?

13
00:01:24,731 --> 00:01:26,566
Tell me the hospital's location.

14
00:02:02,393 --> 00:02:04,020
You go first.

15
00:02:10,944 --> 00:02:11,819
You stopped crying.

16
00:02:19,244 --> 00:02:22,163
You made me stop crying.

17
00:02:23,915 --> 00:02:24,749
Yeah.

18
00:02:27,502 --> 00:02:30,338
If that was your goal, you succeeded.

19
00:02:33,132 --> 00:02:34,509
That's a relief.

20
00:02:36,803 --> 00:02:38,930
That doesn't make it okay.

21
00:02:42,934 --> 00:02:47,355
Though I guess
I did the same thing yesterday.

22
00:02:47,438 --> 00:02:49,148
So I'll just call it even.

23
00:02:49,816 --> 00:02:51,359
Don't ever do that again.

24
00:02:51,442 --> 00:02:53,653
-Why not?
-Huh?

25
00:02:57,407 --> 00:02:59,951
What I meant to say was…

26
00:03:00,451 --> 00:03:05,415
When you've lived together for two years,
you're bound to bump lips all the time.

27
00:03:05,498 --> 00:03:10,169
When you've lived together for two years,
you do this all the time.

28
00:03:10,253 --> 00:03:13,673
-Some days, it gets intense.
-Some days, it gets pretty intense.

29
00:03:13,756 --> 00:03:15,466
And some days, it won't end…

30
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:18,177
And some days,
it doesn't end with just this.

31
00:03:18,261 --> 00:03:21,055
You must be completely insane!

32
00:03:21,889 --> 00:03:25,184
You pretended to be such a gentleman,
but all men are the same.

33
00:03:26,019 --> 00:03:28,980
There's no chance,
so don't even dream about it.

34
00:03:32,108 --> 00:03:33,192
Let's go home.

35
00:03:33,276 --> 00:03:34,777
Excuse me?

36
00:03:35,278 --> 00:03:36,696
You want to take me home?

37
00:03:36,779 --> 00:03:38,072
Then will you live out here?

38
00:03:53,838 --> 00:03:54,672
Eat up.

39
00:03:56,049 --> 00:03:57,884
I heard you didn't eat much today.

40
00:04:06,476 --> 00:04:10,271
I guess you do know
a thing or two about me.

41
00:04:10,772 --> 00:04:11,689
Eat some rice too.

42
00:04:12,774 --> 00:04:14,734
You need a balanced diet
to recover quickly.

43
00:04:15,777 --> 00:04:17,362
Carbs make you gain weight.

44
00:04:17,445 --> 00:04:19,572
It doesn't matter. You'll still be pretty.

45
00:04:29,248 --> 00:04:30,083
This one's cooked.

46
00:04:36,214 --> 00:04:37,799
Aren't you going to eat?

47
00:04:39,050 --> 00:04:40,218
I'm full.

48
00:04:42,553 --> 00:04:43,888
Just eat.

49
00:04:43,971 --> 00:04:47,308
You think I'd be grateful if you said
you were full just watching me eat?

50
00:04:47,392 --> 00:04:48,643
but then have my leftovers?

51
00:04:48,726 --> 00:04:51,854
I really am full.
I had Chinese food earlier.

52
00:05:07,787 --> 00:05:08,621
What?

53
00:05:10,373 --> 00:05:11,749
It's just,

54
00:05:13,042 --> 00:05:14,836
I didn't know you could smile.

55
00:05:31,352 --> 00:05:33,312
I liked you from the moment I saw you.

56
00:05:38,401 --> 00:05:40,236
This one's for real.

57
00:05:45,116 --> 00:05:47,326
Why did he have to wear a suit today?

58
00:05:47,410 --> 00:05:50,288
I wouldn't have flinched
if he was in that scrappy boxer outfit.

59
00:05:51,456 --> 00:05:53,791
I couldn't stop thinking about you.

60
00:05:53,875 --> 00:05:55,209
I just hoped…

61
00:05:57,211 --> 00:05:58,588
to see you again someday.

62
00:05:59,797 --> 00:06:03,926
Seeing you hurt was unbearable.
It killed me.

63
00:06:04,886 --> 00:06:07,555
You're the only woman I've ever liked,

64
00:06:08,598 --> 00:06:10,850
so I don't really know how.

65
00:06:14,896 --> 00:06:17,315
If that look in his eyes was an act,

66
00:06:17,857 --> 00:06:19,567
then he deserves a best actor award.

67
00:06:21,736 --> 00:06:23,738
So he really is my boyfriend?

68
00:06:24,322 --> 00:06:28,201
Then what was that with the toad?
It didn't scare me at all.

69
00:06:28,284 --> 00:06:30,745
I guess you lost your fear
with your memory.

70
00:06:30,828 --> 00:06:34,332
The doctor said head injuries
can cause all sorts of aftereffects.

71
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:39,837
Is that really it?

72
00:06:41,631 --> 00:06:43,007
Did I simply change?

73
00:06:45,134 --> 00:06:47,094
Oh my, Eun-sae?

74
00:06:47,178 --> 00:06:49,680
Go Eun-sae, what's wrong with you?

75
00:06:49,764 --> 00:06:53,059
If you can't wrap your head around it,
you don't have to.

76
00:06:53,142 --> 00:06:55,061
You don't have to believe it.

77
00:06:55,144 --> 00:06:59,232
Don't let those butterflies fool you.

78
00:07:11,702 --> 00:07:13,454
Are you sure the patient is Go Ji-won?

79
00:07:13,538 --> 00:07:15,373
Tell me the hospital's location.

80
00:07:17,959 --> 00:07:20,795
He definitely said "patient"
and "hospital."

81
00:07:22,088 --> 00:07:24,757
The fact that he's scouring hospitals
to find Go Eun-sae

82
00:07:25,633 --> 00:07:28,094
means he thinks she's alive

83
00:07:29,178 --> 00:07:31,305
and doesn't know
Baek Sang-gil dealt with her.

84
00:07:31,806 --> 00:07:33,432
She had these on her.

85
00:07:36,978 --> 00:07:38,563
That man is Mayor Ju's aide.

86
00:07:39,146 --> 00:07:42,149
He went undercover
to gather information on the prosecution.

87
00:07:42,233 --> 00:07:44,902
He's one of us,
so you don't have to worry about him.

88
00:07:48,906 --> 00:07:51,784
The undercover agent is acting on his own.

89
00:07:52,827 --> 00:07:54,370
But why?

90
00:07:55,538 --> 00:07:56,998
How did he know to come here?

91
00:08:02,044 --> 00:08:03,254
KAITO

92
00:08:04,714 --> 00:08:06,799
Hey. Any progress?

93
00:08:07,425 --> 00:08:09,343
We have the stowaway boat's
departure date.

94
00:08:09,844 --> 00:08:11,137
Good work.

95
00:08:11,637 --> 00:08:13,556
Make sure the information doesn't leak.

96
00:08:16,225 --> 00:08:17,977
HONG'S BOXING GYM

97
00:08:18,936 --> 00:08:20,271
What the hell?

98
00:08:20,354 --> 00:08:22,732
I thought he was a mole,
not her real boyfriend.

99
00:08:22,815 --> 00:08:25,026
Why would he be looking for Prosecutor Go?

100
00:08:25,109 --> 00:08:27,820
What's more important
is that he knows about Taffy Village.

101
00:08:27,903 --> 00:08:30,740
I thought this place was safe
and hard to track down, so how…

102
00:08:30,823 --> 00:08:31,657
Hold on.

103
00:08:32,366 --> 00:08:34,201
You said he's been searching hospitals?

104
00:08:34,785 --> 00:08:35,870
What does he look like?

105
00:08:46,422 --> 00:08:49,175
That's him. This guy came here yesterday.

106
00:08:49,258 --> 00:08:50,092
What?

107
00:08:50,176 --> 00:08:53,554
-Are you the head coach here?
-He asked if I was the head coach.

108
00:08:53,638 --> 00:08:56,140
Did you happen to visit
a hospital yesterday?

109
00:08:56,223 --> 00:08:58,351
Then asked if I'd visited the hospital.

110
00:09:01,395 --> 00:09:02,229
You know,

111
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:05,316
since he's managed to track her here,

112
00:09:06,150 --> 00:09:09,236
how about telling Prosecutor Go the truth?

113
00:09:14,241 --> 00:09:15,576
I slept like a baby.

114
00:09:21,499 --> 00:09:22,833
My gosh! Why did I sleep in so late?

115
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:27,630
What's up with you, Eun-sae?

116
00:09:28,381 --> 00:09:31,300
You shouldn't be sleeping
so soundly already.

117
00:09:31,384 --> 00:09:37,556
You should still be suspicious
that all of this might not be true.

118
00:09:39,517 --> 00:09:43,521
We can't just wait around forever
for her memory to come back.

119
00:09:44,397 --> 00:09:46,190
She's suspicious anyway.

120
00:09:46,273 --> 00:09:48,526
Let's just tell her everything.

121
00:09:48,609 --> 00:09:51,028
Tell her that Baek Sang-gil
is no ordinary guy,

122
00:09:51,112 --> 00:09:54,323
so if she wants to stay alive,
she should leave Korea right away.

123
00:09:55,366 --> 00:09:56,867
Let's persuade her like that.

124
00:09:57,868 --> 00:09:58,703
We can't.

125
00:09:58,786 --> 00:09:59,704
Why not?

126
00:09:59,787 --> 00:10:03,332
If she hears all that without her memory,
she'll try to verify it for herself.

127
00:10:03,416 --> 00:10:05,126
Whether she's really a prosecutor.

128
00:10:05,209 --> 00:10:07,712
Whether I'm lying.
She'd try to get to the bottom of it.

129
00:10:09,130 --> 00:10:10,548
She'd be in even more danger.

130
00:10:10,631 --> 00:10:13,968
We could just stop her from doing that.

131
00:10:14,051 --> 00:10:16,303
If someone has no memory of being burned,

132
00:10:16,387 --> 00:10:19,223
no amount of warning
will make them fear fire.

133
00:10:21,934 --> 00:10:24,478
They need to remember
how hot and scary fire is

134
00:10:25,396 --> 00:10:26,939
to know how to avoid it.

135
00:10:30,443 --> 00:10:31,527
Fair enough.

136
00:10:32,069 --> 00:10:34,196
She still doesn't believe you,

137
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:37,658
so even if we tell her all this
and insist she has to leave Korea now,

138
00:10:37,742 --> 00:10:40,619
I doubt she'd just say "Okay,"
and agree to leave.

139
00:10:42,037 --> 00:10:43,080
Goodness.

140
00:10:43,164 --> 00:10:45,541
I guess we need her memory back fast.

141
00:10:46,625 --> 00:10:47,877
We're running out of time.

142
00:10:48,753 --> 00:10:52,089
Kaito called and told me
the stowaway boat leaves in a month.

143
00:10:52,173 --> 00:10:53,966
She needs her memory back before then.

144
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:57,219
Don't we need to do something
about that mole boyfriend?

145
00:10:57,928 --> 00:11:01,807
He even knows about Taffy Village.
Shouldn't we at least distract him?

146
00:11:02,433 --> 00:11:06,061
Baek Sang-gil could keep him at bay
faster and more effectively.

147
00:11:06,145 --> 00:11:10,524
He'd also want to stop anyone
poking around to find Prosecutor Go.

148
00:11:11,817 --> 00:11:12,777
Do you have a plan?

149
00:11:20,701 --> 00:11:23,162
Sending you the detective agency's number.

150
00:11:26,290 --> 00:11:28,626
You were asked
to find someone recently, right?

151
00:11:28,709 --> 00:11:32,546
I'll give you a much easier job
and pay triple the agreed amount.

152
00:11:38,052 --> 00:11:39,762
How childish.

153
00:11:39,845 --> 00:11:41,388
What's with the apples?

154
00:11:41,472 --> 00:11:42,431
BREAKFAST, LUNCH, DINNER

155
00:11:42,515 --> 00:11:44,350
What am I, a kid? Ridiculous.

156
00:12:09,375 --> 00:12:11,752
What are you doing here
so bright and early?

157
00:12:13,254 --> 00:12:14,380
I just…

158
00:12:16,048 --> 00:12:17,007
The reading fee.

159
00:12:18,801 --> 00:12:19,802
Reading fee?

160
00:12:19,885 --> 00:12:21,262
About yesterday…

161
00:12:22,263 --> 00:12:23,556
I was wrong.

162
00:12:25,558 --> 00:12:28,352
It felt like you were insulting my spirit,

163
00:12:28,435 --> 00:12:31,772
and you were so rude and disrespectful,
so I just stood my ground.

164
00:12:31,856 --> 00:12:35,192
I'd rather not receive payment
from a customer who isn't satisfied.

165
00:12:35,276 --> 00:12:36,777
It just doesn't feel right.

166
00:12:39,738 --> 00:12:40,573
Well,

167
00:12:41,073 --> 00:12:43,033
you got there in the end.

168
00:12:43,117 --> 00:12:44,493
That's good.

169
00:12:47,121 --> 00:12:48,372
I'm saying this because

170
00:12:48,455 --> 00:12:52,918
I thought I'd be the bigger person,
even though I really can't stand you…

171
00:12:53,002 --> 00:12:55,546
Come on. Where's this going?

172
00:12:56,046 --> 00:12:56,881
I'm sorry.

173
00:12:59,675 --> 00:13:02,052
-What?
-I said I'm sorry.

174
00:13:02,928 --> 00:13:06,473
As an elder, I shouldn't be fighting
someone who's so much younger than me.

175
00:13:07,975 --> 00:13:09,184
I wasn't at my best.

176
00:13:16,275 --> 00:13:18,193
Well, I also…

177
00:13:22,615 --> 00:13:23,908
apologize for my behavior.

178
00:13:27,912 --> 00:13:29,872
Gosh, you even know how
to lower your head?

179
00:13:29,955 --> 00:13:32,291
When did I lower my head?

180
00:13:32,374 --> 00:13:35,044
Then what was that damn bow?
Or did your neck take over?

181
00:13:35,127 --> 00:13:39,465
"Damn"? Are you here to pick a fight
or apologize? Which is it?

182
00:13:39,548 --> 00:13:40,716
A mix of both. So what?

183
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:45,304
Thanks for giving this back.
You can leave if that's all.

184
00:13:45,387 --> 00:13:49,099
Don't you worry.
I'll leave even if you beg me not to.

185
00:13:57,232 --> 00:13:58,275
Madam Shaman.

186
00:14:02,905 --> 00:14:06,325
I'm giving you this because I also thought
I'd be the bigger person,

187
00:14:06,408 --> 00:14:07,785
even though I can't stand you.

188
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:25,302
Absolutely ridiculous.

189
00:14:27,554 --> 00:14:29,890
Well, I guess she is an elder.

190
00:14:29,974 --> 00:14:32,643
She looked like
she'd never back down yesterday.

191
00:14:32,726 --> 00:14:33,894
What's gotten into her?

192
00:14:41,026 --> 00:14:44,071
Hey, I apologized just now.

193
00:14:44,571 --> 00:14:48,283
I even gave back the fee because I felt
uneasy about accepting your money.

194
00:14:49,201 --> 00:14:52,871
I've been downing cups of ice-cold water,

195
00:14:53,455 --> 00:14:55,582
but I'm still fuming inside.

196
00:14:56,291 --> 00:14:58,502
Tae-ha, you should really reconsider.

197
00:14:58,585 --> 00:15:00,921
If you take in a woman like that
as your wife,

198
00:15:01,005 --> 00:15:03,632
your life could go up in smoke.

199
00:15:08,637 --> 00:15:10,764
-This should be enough.
-What are you doing?

200
00:15:10,848 --> 00:15:13,017
For the broken Bodhisattva statue.

201
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:15,185
-How can you…
-Please accept it.

202
00:15:17,104 --> 00:15:18,022
I'm sorry.

203
00:15:21,233 --> 00:15:25,195
And please apologize to Eun-sae.

204
00:15:26,864 --> 00:15:29,867
Instead of bringing her here
to apologize to me,

205
00:15:29,950 --> 00:15:32,119
you want me to go
and apologize to that brat?

206
00:15:32,202 --> 00:15:34,496
I heard that you grabbed her hair.

207
00:15:35,372 --> 00:15:37,374
-But--
-That's assault.

208
00:15:38,292 --> 00:15:39,293
Well, that was--

209
00:15:39,376 --> 00:15:41,295
You frowned on my becoming a thug.

210
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:46,300
You despise violence,
yet you resorted to it.

211
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:49,136
So please apologize.

212
00:15:49,803 --> 00:15:53,140
What about her disrespecting her elders
without knowing her place?

213
00:15:53,223 --> 00:15:55,309
If you apologize first as her elder,

214
00:15:55,809 --> 00:15:56,977
she'll follow suit.

215
00:15:57,061 --> 00:16:01,148
Right, I'm sure
that brat would do just that.

216
00:16:01,648 --> 00:16:02,691
I'm certain she will.

217
00:16:02,775 --> 00:16:05,277
She's just not in her right mind
following the accident.

218
00:16:06,028 --> 00:16:07,071
She's a good person.

219
00:16:07,154 --> 00:16:10,032
Do you look at people with a blindfold on?

220
00:16:10,115 --> 00:16:12,618
How can you be
such a bad judge of character?

221
00:16:14,953 --> 00:16:15,954
I know that

222
00:16:17,039 --> 00:16:18,499
you're also a good person.

223
00:16:20,125 --> 00:16:21,001
What's that now?

224
00:16:22,836 --> 00:16:24,046
I still remember

225
00:16:24,546 --> 00:16:26,090
how you'd give me rice cakes

226
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:29,343
whenever you ran into me
on my way home from school.

227
00:16:30,844 --> 00:16:34,556
And how you used to stuff my pockets
with boiled eggs,

228
00:16:35,057 --> 00:16:37,226
saying that athletes shouldn't go hungry.

229
00:16:37,810 --> 00:16:39,520
Thanks to you, I was a good athlete.

230
00:16:44,024 --> 00:16:44,900
Thank you.

231
00:16:46,026 --> 00:16:47,945
Why are you saying all that now?

232
00:16:48,654 --> 00:16:50,614
You're saying whatever for your girl.

233
00:16:55,369 --> 00:16:56,537
I'd really appreciate it.

234
00:17:00,874 --> 00:17:01,917
What about dinner?

235
00:17:03,335 --> 00:17:04,419
Have you eaten?

236
00:17:06,004 --> 00:17:08,465
I made some red bean rice cakes
last night.

237
00:17:09,133 --> 00:17:09,967
I'll pack some up.

238
00:17:24,398 --> 00:17:26,942
Since I have this,
I guess I could color it in.

239
00:17:37,703 --> 00:17:40,539
Eat breakfast, done

240
00:17:40,622 --> 00:17:43,208
Eat dinner, done

241
00:17:43,292 --> 00:17:46,670
When I opened the window…

242
00:17:51,842 --> 00:17:52,801
You're up.

243
00:17:53,385 --> 00:17:56,847
I've been up for a while.
It's not like the bed is comfortable.

244
00:18:01,935 --> 00:18:04,938
That shaman lady came by earlier.

245
00:18:06,148 --> 00:18:07,065
She did?

246
00:18:07,149 --> 00:18:08,942
She apologized and even paid me back.

247
00:18:10,110 --> 00:18:10,944
That's good.

248
00:18:11,028 --> 00:18:15,908
I guess I'm not the type
to be hated for long.

249
00:18:19,578 --> 00:18:20,829
If you're done eating, let's go.

250
00:18:21,830 --> 00:18:22,664
Where to?

251
00:18:22,748 --> 00:18:24,416
The clinic you went to yesterday.

252
00:18:24,499 --> 00:18:27,044
You need treatment
to get your memory back fast.

253
00:18:28,462 --> 00:18:29,296
Get ready.

254
00:18:33,842 --> 00:18:36,220
What was that? If this is all a lie,

255
00:18:36,303 --> 00:18:38,555
shouldn't he be hoping
I don't regain my memory?

256
00:18:38,639 --> 00:18:41,141
Then why is he so eager to help me
get my memory back?

257
00:18:41,225 --> 00:18:43,560
Is he really my boyfriend?

258
00:18:46,146 --> 00:18:48,523
Why don't you try selling stuff
on Instagram too?

259
00:18:48,607 --> 00:18:51,777
I bet you could get followers
and become an influencer in no time.

260
00:18:52,402 --> 00:18:53,403
No, I couldn't.

261
00:18:53,904 --> 00:18:55,405
Have you forgotten who you are?

262
00:18:55,489 --> 00:18:59,243
You're the legendary Min Su-ji
who ruled beauty forums back in the day.

263
00:18:59,326 --> 00:19:00,577
Right, Dr. An?

264
00:19:00,661 --> 00:19:02,371
Yeah, back in the day.

265
00:19:09,670 --> 00:19:11,713
I'm going to go brush my teeth.

266
00:19:21,348 --> 00:19:23,183
Hey, can we talk…

267
00:19:23,684 --> 00:19:25,352
How long will you keep this up?

268
00:19:27,562 --> 00:19:30,315
I told you that I had no choice
but to go on that blind date.

269
00:19:30,399 --> 00:19:32,818
I told you that my parents and I
run on give-and-take.

270
00:19:33,318 --> 00:19:37,572
They set up this clinic for me,
so I have to follow their wishes somewhat.

271
00:19:37,656 --> 00:19:40,575
I kept refusing until now,
and I only went on one date.

272
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:44,621
Exactly.

273
00:19:45,122 --> 00:19:45,956
What?

274
00:19:46,039 --> 00:19:49,751
You kept refusing, but you never told them
that you have a girlfriend.

275
00:19:49,835 --> 00:19:50,669
That's because--

276
00:19:50,752 --> 00:19:53,672
At the clinic and with your parents,
you always hide me.

277
00:19:54,298 --> 00:19:57,718
You say it's because of what the staff
or your parents might say,

278
00:19:57,801 --> 00:19:59,011
but the truth is,

279
00:19:59,094 --> 00:20:01,221
I'm just not good enough for you, am I?

280
00:20:01,305 --> 00:20:03,807
-How could you say--
-Not some nurse's aide.

281
00:20:03,890 --> 00:20:07,185
You want to meet a woman
fit for a clinic director, don't you?

282
00:20:11,231 --> 00:20:12,691
Then what about you?

283
00:20:12,774 --> 00:20:15,694
If you felt that way,
why are you still with me?

284
00:20:16,278 --> 00:20:18,322
It's because I own a clinic, isn't it?

285
00:20:23,076 --> 00:20:26,330
-So I've decided to know my place.
-What's that supposed to mean?

286
00:20:27,581 --> 00:20:30,876
I'm saying we should break up.
You're free to go on those blind dates.

287
00:20:30,959 --> 00:20:33,003
I'll find a man who's more on my level.

288
00:20:34,338 --> 00:20:35,339
Hey, Min Su-ji.

289
00:20:36,965 --> 00:20:38,300
-Su-ji.
-Hello.

290
00:20:40,218 --> 00:20:41,636
This is the director.

291
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:44,556
Here. I brought him.
Someone to vouch for my identity.

292
00:20:46,099 --> 00:20:47,351
Nice to meet you.

293
00:20:47,851 --> 00:20:49,478
What's with the "nice to meet you"?

294
00:20:50,395 --> 00:20:53,190
-He said you were classmates.
-Classmates?

295
00:20:54,316 --> 00:20:56,360
Long time no see, Jang Tae-ha.

296
00:21:06,661 --> 00:21:08,830
All right, 1,000 won for a round!

297
00:21:08,914 --> 00:21:10,707
Come play balloon toss!

298
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:17,839
-Wow, Min Su-ji is so pretty.
-No wonder she's Internet famous.

299
00:21:17,923 --> 00:21:20,258
Wow, she's a goddess.
The "it" girl of Gujin.

300
00:21:20,342 --> 00:21:21,802
She's glowing.

301
00:21:27,391 --> 00:21:31,269
AN GI-JUN

302
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:37,609
Get your makeup done here!

303
00:21:38,610 --> 00:21:39,611
Here's your yulmu tea.

304
00:21:41,279 --> 00:21:44,658
Thanks. I just love yulmu tea.

305
00:21:51,665 --> 00:21:52,958
It's boiling today.

306
00:21:55,377 --> 00:21:56,878
Should we get drinks? Cola?

307
00:21:56,962 --> 00:21:58,547
-Cola sounds good.
-Sure.

308
00:21:58,630 --> 00:22:01,049
Hey, can we get three colas?

309
00:22:01,133 --> 00:22:02,300
Sure.

310
00:22:19,484 --> 00:22:21,278
Wipe your sweat with this.

311
00:22:22,612 --> 00:22:23,447
Thanks.

312
00:22:27,409 --> 00:22:28,994
What was your name again?

313
00:22:30,162 --> 00:22:31,913
Su… Sun-deok?

314
00:22:32,873 --> 00:22:35,250
That would be me.

315
00:22:36,585 --> 00:22:38,920
It's Su-ji. Min Su-ji.

316
00:22:39,004 --> 00:22:40,755
Of course. Thanks, Min Su-ji.

317
00:23:04,696 --> 00:23:06,281
DIRECTOR AN GI-JUN

318
00:23:06,364 --> 00:23:07,824
Oh, come on.

319
00:23:10,202 --> 00:23:11,745
Our nurses are so clumsy.

320
00:23:11,828 --> 00:23:13,038
Can I take a card?

321
00:23:13,121 --> 00:23:14,539
Sure, please do.

322
00:23:17,417 --> 00:23:19,628
Looking at this, I think I remember.

323
00:23:20,337 --> 00:23:22,714
Weren't you the guy
who always got the best grades?

324
00:23:24,007 --> 00:23:25,425
Well, not always.

325
00:23:25,509 --> 00:23:27,594
You were so smart,
and now you're a doctor.

326
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:30,347
And how are you doing these days?

327
00:23:30,430 --> 00:23:33,517
I heard you got into something else
after you gave up boxing.

328
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:34,893
I left that job recently.

329
00:23:36,186 --> 00:23:37,437
I see.

330
00:23:38,647 --> 00:23:40,732
Ms. Go Eun-sae told me
about her situation.

331
00:23:40,815 --> 00:23:43,026
But our hospital has regulations.

332
00:23:43,109 --> 00:23:45,153
-If a person's unverified, we can't--
-Thanks.

333
00:23:46,613 --> 00:23:47,948
You'll treat her, won't you?

334
00:23:49,032 --> 00:23:50,242
Otherwise, you wouldn't have called.

335
00:23:51,284 --> 00:23:53,078
Right, yeah.

336
00:23:54,037 --> 00:23:57,874
I'll pay whatever it costs,
so please do what you can for her.

337
00:23:58,500 --> 00:23:59,501
Okay.

338
00:24:00,168 --> 00:24:03,338
-It's a good thing I'm the director--
-Exactly.

339
00:24:05,215 --> 00:24:08,260
So these are the perks
of having a capable classmate.

340
00:24:09,970 --> 00:24:10,845
Thanks in advance.

341
00:24:12,222 --> 00:24:13,348
Yeah, sure.

342
00:24:17,852 --> 00:24:20,021
What are they talking about for so long?

343
00:24:21,982 --> 00:24:22,941
You're beautiful.

344
00:24:24,317 --> 00:24:26,486
Do you have a boyfriend?

345
00:24:26,570 --> 00:24:27,445
I'm sorry, but…

346
00:24:27,529 --> 00:24:29,281
I do. I'm sorry.

347
00:24:29,364 --> 00:24:31,575
Understood. My apologies.

348
00:24:38,081 --> 00:24:39,082
Here you go.

349
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,209
It's okay.

350
00:24:41,293 --> 00:24:43,795
I only drink coffee
that's been freshly roasted.

351
00:25:09,988 --> 00:25:12,657
-How did it go?
-You'll come twice a week for treatment.

352
00:25:14,034 --> 00:25:14,868
Really?

353
00:25:15,785 --> 00:25:19,164
Ms. Go Eun-sae, we'll start with an EEG
and some basic tests today.

354
00:25:19,247 --> 00:25:20,373
Please come this way.

355
00:25:20,874 --> 00:25:21,708
Okay.

356
00:25:22,375 --> 00:25:24,544
-Good luck with the tests.
-Okay.

357
00:25:44,606 --> 00:25:47,609
If I'd known he was coming,
I would have put in an extra insole.

358
00:25:48,109 --> 00:25:50,195
Come on, Gi-jun.

359
00:25:51,321 --> 00:25:53,698
You always look so handsome,
but today of all days,

360
00:25:54,282 --> 00:25:56,034
why do you look so shabby?

361
00:26:14,511 --> 00:26:15,637
Hold up, An Gi-jun.

362
00:26:16,221 --> 00:26:17,305
Have some dignity.

363
00:26:19,265 --> 00:26:21,935
You have nothing to feel small about
anymore, okay?

364
00:26:22,018 --> 00:26:23,687
Jang Tae-ha is a former thug,

365
00:26:24,187 --> 00:26:25,397
and you're a doctor.

366
00:26:26,564 --> 00:26:28,650
You're on a different level, okay?

367
00:26:28,733 --> 00:26:31,736
If Su-ji has any sense,
she won't be interested in him anymore.

368
00:26:31,820 --> 00:26:34,864
Seriously, what is there to see in him?

369
00:26:37,909 --> 00:26:39,494
It's been a while, Jang Tae-ha.

370
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:46,584
Don't you remember me?

371
00:26:47,168 --> 00:26:48,920
We were classmates in high school.

372
00:26:49,003 --> 00:26:50,630
Before you moved to Seoul.

373
00:26:51,339 --> 00:26:52,465
Right.

374
00:26:54,509 --> 00:26:55,677
Right!

375
00:26:57,721 --> 00:26:58,805
Su…

376
00:26:59,973 --> 00:27:00,807
Sun-deok?

377
00:27:03,685 --> 00:27:06,187
It's Su-ji. Min Su-ji.

378
00:27:06,896 --> 00:27:08,356
Right. Sorry.

379
00:27:14,654 --> 00:27:15,822
Are you back in Gujin?

380
00:27:16,948 --> 00:27:18,783
Yeah, I live in Taffy Village.

381
00:27:18,867 --> 00:27:19,909
With your girlfriend?

382
00:27:19,993 --> 00:27:20,994
Yeah.

383
00:27:29,377 --> 00:27:30,628
Hey, Go Eun-sae.

384
00:27:31,755 --> 00:27:32,589
Are you okay?

385
00:27:32,672 --> 00:27:35,008
I'm fine. I just stubbed my toe.

386
00:27:35,091 --> 00:27:37,886
-Does it hurt a lot? Can you walk?
-I'm fine.

387
00:27:38,386 --> 00:27:41,389
Stop overreacting.
People would think I lost a foot.

388
00:27:41,473 --> 00:27:43,266
-You should be more careful.
-Hold on.

389
00:27:50,565 --> 00:27:54,444
Once we have the results,
we'll start the treatment next week.

390
00:27:54,527 --> 00:27:58,198
We'll do a drug test, then begin
cognitive rehabilitation therapy.

391
00:27:58,281 --> 00:27:59,908
Thanks. I appreciate it.

392
00:27:59,991 --> 00:28:01,159
No need to thank me.

393
00:28:01,242 --> 00:28:02,160
God bless you.

394
00:28:07,248 --> 00:28:08,249
We'll get going, then.

395
00:28:08,333 --> 00:28:09,751
-Okay.
-Bye, Ji-su.

396
00:28:10,335 --> 00:28:12,837
It's… Su-ji.

397
00:28:22,764 --> 00:28:24,557
You seem happy to see your first love.

398
00:28:25,225 --> 00:28:26,059
Yeah.

399
00:28:26,142 --> 00:28:29,270
It looks like Jang Tae-ha's still got it.

400
00:28:38,112 --> 00:28:41,115
That woman earlier.
She was your classmate?

401
00:28:41,199 --> 00:28:43,660
-Yeah.
-I see.

402
00:28:44,536 --> 00:28:47,121
Well, she was… a bit pretty.

403
00:28:49,582 --> 00:28:52,919
With today's beauty techniques,

404
00:28:53,002 --> 00:28:55,296
almost anyone can look like her
with a little effort.

405
00:28:55,380 --> 00:28:57,841
It's only because I'm wearing
these tacky clothes,

406
00:28:57,924 --> 00:29:00,093
but if I dressed up, I'd be a knockout.

407
00:29:01,261 --> 00:29:02,470
Should we go shopping?

408
00:29:03,638 --> 00:29:05,098
There's a mall in town.

409
00:29:20,363 --> 00:29:22,240
-What do you think?
-It's pretty.

410
00:29:26,244 --> 00:29:28,371
-How about this one?
-It's pretty.

411
00:29:32,292 --> 00:29:33,293
How about this?

412
00:29:38,131 --> 00:29:38,965
It's pretty.

413
00:29:40,925 --> 00:29:44,762
Stop saying "it's pretty"
without meaning it.

414
00:29:45,263 --> 00:29:46,848
I do mean it.

415
00:29:49,767 --> 00:29:51,394
You looked pretty in every single one.

416
00:30:06,242 --> 00:30:08,453
How can you say that so casually?

417
00:30:25,136 --> 00:30:26,179
It's true though.

418
00:30:33,061 --> 00:30:34,771
You already put a pink one in here.

419
00:30:35,688 --> 00:30:38,441
That was coral pink.
This one is bright pink.

420
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:40,276
They're different?

421
00:30:41,277 --> 00:30:45,073
Of course they are.
No two shades are ever the same.

422
00:30:45,156 --> 00:30:46,658
You really are clueless.

423
00:30:49,452 --> 00:30:51,162
This one's moist. I like it.

424
00:30:51,746 --> 00:30:54,624
And the ingredients look good too.

425
00:30:57,335 --> 00:30:58,419
One of those.

426
00:31:01,756 --> 00:31:03,591
I think that's enough for makeup.

427
00:31:05,969 --> 00:31:07,178
You know…

428
00:31:09,764 --> 00:31:11,766
There's one last thing that I need.

429
00:31:24,862 --> 00:31:26,698
Now I feel like I can breathe.

430
00:31:26,781 --> 00:31:30,076
A modern person needs a phone, after all.

431
00:31:30,159 --> 00:31:33,079
It's a shame
that it's registered under your name,

432
00:31:33,997 --> 00:31:35,665
but I guess it can't be helped.

433
00:31:37,917 --> 00:31:39,335
You look happy.

434
00:31:39,419 --> 00:31:41,587
Yes, today isn't so bad.

435
00:31:42,255 --> 00:31:45,383
We agreed that I'd get treatment,
I got a phone,

436
00:31:45,466 --> 00:31:46,718
and I went shopping.

437
00:31:46,801 --> 00:31:49,095
That was such a stress reliever.

438
00:31:50,388 --> 00:31:52,265
Let's see.

439
00:31:52,348 --> 00:31:53,349
Huh?

440
00:31:54,559 --> 00:31:56,019
I only picked up one of these.

441
00:31:56,728 --> 00:31:58,521
Did you add the rest of them?

442
00:31:59,564 --> 00:32:01,399
Yeah, you said it was good.

443
00:32:04,318 --> 00:32:06,195
I can't believe you.

444
00:32:06,279 --> 00:32:08,281
You didn't have to be so thoughtful.

445
00:32:08,865 --> 00:32:10,742
I have a small face,

446
00:32:10,825 --> 00:32:14,078
so one cushion foundation
lasts me a long time.

447
00:32:14,162 --> 00:32:15,580
When will I use all this up?

448
00:32:17,457 --> 00:32:18,791
They're not for you.

449
00:32:20,043 --> 00:32:21,544
Then who are they for?

450
00:32:22,670 --> 00:32:23,671
I heard this is good.

451
00:32:24,297 --> 00:32:26,257
-One for each of you.
-What's this?

452
00:32:30,928 --> 00:32:36,392
If I use this,
I'll really look as pretty as a new bride.

453
00:32:36,893 --> 00:32:38,478
Right, honey?

454
00:32:39,145 --> 00:32:41,564
Of course.
You'll be the prettiest girl in town.

455
00:32:42,565 --> 00:32:44,067
Wait a minute.

456
00:32:46,152 --> 00:32:49,447
One second. That's not how you use it.

457
00:32:49,530 --> 00:32:50,865
I'll show you how to use it.

458
00:32:50,948 --> 00:32:53,701
You only need a slight dab.

459
00:32:54,368 --> 00:32:55,536
I'll put it on for you.

460
00:32:56,037 --> 00:33:00,166
Like this. Just tap like this, and then…

461
00:33:00,750 --> 00:33:04,003
Tap, tap.

462
00:33:04,962 --> 00:33:07,381
Tap gently.

463
00:33:07,465 --> 00:33:08,800
Just like this.

464
00:33:11,594 --> 00:33:14,472
Your face looks brighter
just from evening out your skin tone.

465
00:33:15,723 --> 00:33:16,933
Wait a minute.

466
00:33:20,728 --> 00:33:22,188
Goodness me.

467
00:33:22,271 --> 00:33:26,109
Why are there so many different
colored powders to put on your face?

468
00:33:26,192 --> 00:33:28,569
I think this will look good on you.
One second.

469
00:33:29,070 --> 00:33:30,071
-Here.
-More?

470
00:33:30,154 --> 00:33:32,156
Just a little more of this.

471
00:33:33,699 --> 00:33:34,784
Okay.

472
00:33:34,867 --> 00:33:36,119
Wow, that's pretty.

473
00:33:36,202 --> 00:33:38,162
-Let me see.
-You look so pretty.

474
00:33:38,246 --> 00:33:39,705
Good heavens!

475
00:33:39,789 --> 00:33:44,001
My face looks so rosy and healthy.

476
00:33:44,669 --> 00:33:45,962
Isn't that right?

477
00:33:46,045 --> 00:33:48,798
This looks good on you,
so I'll give it to you as a gift.

478
00:33:48,881 --> 00:33:50,216
Use it from now on.

479
00:33:50,299 --> 00:33:53,845
-And for you, Song-wol…
-How lovely.

480
00:33:53,928 --> 00:33:54,762
This one.

481
00:34:05,273 --> 00:34:06,107
Thanks for today.

482
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:08,234
For what?

483
00:34:08,734 --> 00:34:09,819
For dolling Grandma up.

484
00:34:11,112 --> 00:34:13,447
I never knew she was so pretty.

485
00:34:14,031 --> 00:34:15,491
You really like your grandma.

486
00:34:17,493 --> 00:34:18,661
Because she's my grandma.

487
00:34:22,623 --> 00:34:24,375
-Hello, Coach.
-Hey, Pil-seung.

488
00:34:24,458 --> 00:34:26,794
-Are you training hard?
-Yes, I am.

489
00:34:26,878 --> 00:34:28,379
-Good.
-I'll be going now.

490
00:34:28,462 --> 00:34:29,380
See you.

491
00:34:32,383 --> 00:34:33,259
Who was that?

492
00:34:33,759 --> 00:34:35,761
Ms. Pang's son. He goes to our gym.

493
00:34:35,845 --> 00:34:37,597
Who's Ms. Pang?

494
00:34:37,680 --> 00:34:40,641
A woman who hangs out
with the shaman lady--

495
00:34:41,350 --> 00:34:44,562
You mean the S.E.S of Taffy Village?

496
00:34:45,229 --> 00:34:46,230
Their leader.

497
00:34:46,898 --> 00:34:48,524
That lady.

498
00:34:50,443 --> 00:34:53,821
Her son is handsome.
He doesn't take after his mom at all.

499
00:34:54,488 --> 00:34:57,909
Don't tell anyone in the village
that Pil-seung goes to our gym.

500
00:34:57,992 --> 00:34:58,826
It's a secret.

501
00:34:59,493 --> 00:35:01,537
Who would I talk to in this village?

502
00:35:02,205 --> 00:35:04,081
I don't have a single friend here.

503
00:35:04,665 --> 00:35:08,461
Speaking of friends, you really don't know
any of their numbers?

504
00:35:09,253 --> 00:35:12,840
Wasn't there anyone I would
meet often when we lived in Seoul?

505
00:35:14,008 --> 00:35:16,427
I don't know.
You didn't talk about your friends much.

506
00:35:16,510 --> 00:35:19,805
But I must have had at least one friend.

507
00:35:24,602 --> 00:35:28,105
Why aren't my friends looking for me?

508
00:35:38,032 --> 00:35:39,575
We're closed for the…

509
00:35:39,659 --> 00:35:40,743
Hello.

510
00:35:45,623 --> 00:35:47,124
-Here.
-Thank you.

511
00:35:49,794 --> 00:35:51,921
She didn't contact you either?

512
00:35:52,713 --> 00:35:56,300
She didn't.
The last time we went shopping together,

513
00:35:56,384 --> 00:35:59,387
Ji-won got a little upset with me
about something.

514
00:35:59,470 --> 00:36:03,266
At first, I thought she wasn't
reaching out because she was still mad.

515
00:36:04,350 --> 00:36:07,645
But even after that, I couldn't
get through to her by phone or by text.

516
00:36:08,562 --> 00:36:11,274
So I was planning
to report her missing tomorrow.

517
00:36:11,816 --> 00:36:15,611
She's not missing. She had applied
for a long-term leave of absence.

518
00:36:16,237 --> 00:36:18,030
-Long-term leave?
-Yes.

519
00:36:18,114 --> 00:36:20,449
I don't know what drove her to do that,

520
00:36:21,033 --> 00:36:24,620
but if you hear from Ji-won,
please let me know.

521
00:36:27,540 --> 00:36:28,916
Okay, I will.

522
00:36:40,553 --> 00:36:41,971
DETECTIVE AGENCY

523
00:36:43,180 --> 00:36:45,349
Yes, have you found Go Ji-won?

524
00:36:51,314 --> 00:36:52,315
Thank you.

525
00:36:52,398 --> 00:36:54,692
Why did you ask to meet
in a place like this?

526
00:36:55,693 --> 00:36:57,862
We're not close enough
to share a meal, are we?

527
00:36:57,945 --> 00:37:02,074
The longer I search,
the more I realize it's no ordinary task.

528
00:37:02,158 --> 00:37:04,076
We can't report her missing,

529
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:06,329
and finding someone
through unofficial channels

530
00:37:06,412 --> 00:37:08,914
is a rather discreet and important task.

531
00:37:08,998 --> 00:37:11,584
This kind of thing
isn't a walk in the park.

532
00:37:11,667 --> 00:37:13,210
What is it you're trying to say?

533
00:37:13,961 --> 00:37:16,630
I'd like to renegotiate the down payment.

534
00:37:18,758 --> 00:37:23,012
So you called me out here
to ask for more money?

535
00:37:23,095 --> 00:37:27,266
For large-scale jobs,
we don't cut corners on formalities.

536
00:37:31,896 --> 00:37:33,898
So committed to formalities, aren't you?

537
00:37:55,336 --> 00:37:56,170
Yes.

538
00:37:57,421 --> 00:37:58,964
Thank you for your work.

539
00:38:01,133 --> 00:38:02,927
DETECTIVE AGENCY

540
00:38:24,573 --> 00:38:26,784
BREAKFAST, LUNCH, DINNER

541
00:38:29,578 --> 00:38:30,663
She took all her meds.

542
00:38:37,253 --> 00:38:40,256
Like this. Just tap like this, and then…

543
00:38:40,339 --> 00:38:41,841
There we go.

544
00:39:26,093 --> 00:39:29,513
I told you to lie low.
Look where that got you.

545
00:39:30,473 --> 00:39:33,642
She did me a favor by disappearing
voluntarily. Why try to find her?

546
00:39:36,270 --> 00:39:37,480
Still,

547
00:39:38,564 --> 00:39:41,817
why must you go this far…

548
00:39:48,115 --> 00:39:50,159
The best way to grow an apple tree…

549
00:39:55,623 --> 00:39:57,249
is to cut off the buds

550
00:39:58,334 --> 00:39:59,543
that are bothersome.

551
00:40:06,342 --> 00:40:08,761
"What if I let this one be?"

552
00:40:09,470 --> 00:40:13,557
"What if I let it grow a little
and then cut it off?"

553
00:40:14,225 --> 00:40:15,518
A moment's hesitation…

554
00:40:18,312 --> 00:40:19,939
could ruin your entire harvest.

555
00:40:23,692 --> 00:40:24,985
No, but…

556
00:40:27,071 --> 00:40:28,656
Wait, hold on.

557
00:40:28,739 --> 00:40:29,782
Wait.

558
00:40:29,865 --> 00:40:32,326
Please don't kill me. Wait, please.

559
00:40:32,409 --> 00:40:34,078
No, wait.

560
00:40:34,662 --> 00:40:35,746
Hold on.

561
00:40:35,829 --> 00:40:37,206
Please, no!

562
00:40:38,499 --> 00:40:40,084
There's more than just the watch!

563
00:40:40,918 --> 00:40:42,378
It's not just the watch.

564
00:40:45,839 --> 00:40:47,341
There's one more thing.

565
00:40:48,217 --> 00:40:51,720
Prosecutor Go said she had prepared
one more thing besides the watch.

566
00:40:51,804 --> 00:40:54,014
That's what I was looking for.

567
00:40:54,515 --> 00:40:59,144
If I'm alive, and if Ji-won…
I mean, if Prosecutor Go is alive,

568
00:40:59,228 --> 00:41:02,565
surely I could be of use to you later on?

569
00:41:07,778 --> 00:41:08,946
Please don't kill me.

570
00:41:35,848 --> 00:41:36,682
What is it?

571
00:41:41,103 --> 00:41:42,021
You put makeup on.

572
00:41:43,105 --> 00:41:45,733
I bought so much yesterday,
so I should use it.

573
00:41:46,525 --> 00:41:48,319
Don't go falling for me.

574
00:41:54,325 --> 00:41:55,576
As if I could help it.

575
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:04,627
It's so good.

576
00:42:07,254 --> 00:42:08,464
Oh, right.

577
00:42:09,840 --> 00:42:11,133
Let's go to Seoul.

578
00:42:12,676 --> 00:42:14,511
We lived there longer than here.

579
00:42:14,595 --> 00:42:17,806
I might remember something
if we go back to where we lived.

580
00:42:17,890 --> 00:42:18,849
We can't do that.

581
00:42:20,434 --> 00:42:21,435
Why not?

582
00:42:23,145 --> 00:42:24,396
You're not

583
00:42:25,522 --> 00:42:27,441
fully recovered for a long trip like that.

584
00:42:29,026 --> 00:42:31,487
It's not like we'd be going
to the other side of the world.

585
00:42:31,570 --> 00:42:33,572
It's only a few hours away.

586
00:42:34,490 --> 00:42:36,492
We don't have many good memories in Seoul.

587
00:42:37,451 --> 00:42:39,495
It'll just make us feel bad.

588
00:42:40,120 --> 00:42:43,791
Good or bad,
I need to find whatever memories I can--

589
00:42:43,874 --> 00:42:44,833
How about a ride?

590
00:42:46,293 --> 00:42:48,754
-What?
-You liked riding scooters.

591
00:42:50,297 --> 00:42:51,131
I did?

592
00:42:51,215 --> 00:42:53,258
Whenever you were stressed,
you'd go riding.

593
00:42:54,760 --> 00:42:58,305
You should try it.
It might help you remember something.

594
00:43:02,518 --> 00:43:03,435
Scooters?

595
00:43:10,067 --> 00:43:13,696
Why does this feel so familiar?

596
00:43:17,241 --> 00:43:18,409
Okay, let's start slow--

597
00:43:20,035 --> 00:43:21,203
I know this.

598
00:43:21,704 --> 00:43:23,622
Yes, I know this!

599
00:43:23,706 --> 00:43:24,998
I know this, I do!

600
00:43:25,499 --> 00:43:26,750
-Hold on tight.
-Careful.

601
00:43:32,881 --> 00:43:34,466
I'm good at this.

602
00:43:36,552 --> 00:43:38,262
No way.

603
00:43:38,846 --> 00:43:40,681
This feels great!

604
00:44:11,128 --> 00:44:12,755
Are they filming an action movie?

605
00:44:12,838 --> 00:44:15,340
Why are they speeding around
the village on a scooter?

606
00:44:15,424 --> 00:44:18,635
Exactly. Why are they speeding
when no one's even chasing them?

607
00:44:18,719 --> 00:44:19,845
Leave them be.

608
00:44:19,928 --> 00:44:22,973
-They're still in the honeymoon phase.
-That's the honeymoon phase?

609
00:44:23,056 --> 00:44:26,518
When it looks like shenanigans
from the outside

610
00:44:26,602 --> 00:44:28,103
but makes perfect sense to them.

611
00:44:28,187 --> 00:44:29,396
That's dating for you.

612
00:44:29,480 --> 00:44:32,983
I wouldn't know. The last time
I felt love in the air was in a past life.

613
00:44:36,528 --> 00:44:38,781
Oh, enough with that.
Let's go do our hair.

614
00:44:38,864 --> 00:44:39,823
-Let's go.
-Let's.

615
00:44:39,907 --> 00:44:41,742
-Just one last drink.
-Yes.

616
00:44:41,825 --> 00:44:42,743
Cheers!

617
00:44:52,044 --> 00:44:53,045
Awesome!

618
00:44:54,546 --> 00:44:57,424
This is so cool.
Why am I so good at riding a scooter?

619
00:44:57,508 --> 00:44:59,134
You said you'd done courier work.

620
00:44:59,218 --> 00:45:00,052
I did?

621
00:45:01,136 --> 00:45:02,012
Remember anything?

622
00:45:05,724 --> 00:45:06,683
I don't.

623
00:45:07,267 --> 00:45:10,270
But I can tell
I was good at riding scooters.

624
00:45:10,354 --> 00:45:12,898
My body remembers.

625
00:45:13,941 --> 00:45:14,900
What else did I like?

626
00:45:15,484 --> 00:45:16,318
What?

627
00:45:16,401 --> 00:45:18,946
Tell me more. I want to keep finding out.

628
00:45:24,284 --> 00:45:25,410
Taking pictures.

629
00:45:26,245 --> 00:45:27,120
Pictures?

630
00:45:48,892 --> 00:45:50,519
How do I look?

631
00:45:53,021 --> 00:45:55,274
Come on, it looks like I'm planted there.

632
00:45:55,357 --> 00:45:59,027
What's with these proportions?
My legs look so short!

633
00:46:02,948 --> 00:46:04,074
Look closely.

634
00:46:04,157 --> 00:46:09,288
Take it so that my feet are one centimeter
above the bottom of the screen.

635
00:46:09,371 --> 00:46:11,707
That way, my legs will look longer.

636
00:46:14,459 --> 00:46:15,961
How do I know these details?

637
00:46:17,212 --> 00:46:19,131
I told you that you liked taking pictures.

638
00:46:23,427 --> 00:46:26,305
Anyway, take it again. One centimeter!

639
00:46:44,531 --> 00:46:48,493
Well, that's a new level of ridiculous.

640
00:46:48,577 --> 00:46:52,539
Will it kill her to look at the camera?

641
00:46:52,623 --> 00:46:55,250
She's dead set on avoiding the camera.

642
00:46:55,334 --> 00:46:58,211
When did he become
such a hopeless romantic?

643
00:46:58,295 --> 00:47:02,007
He'll do whatever his wife asks him to do.

644
00:47:03,216 --> 00:47:05,469
-Why do we even bother?
-Such an eyesore.

645
00:47:05,552 --> 00:47:06,386
Let's go.

646
00:47:13,226 --> 00:47:15,854
Some of these
might actually be worth keeping.

647
00:47:16,355 --> 00:47:18,774
But I really don't remember any of this.

648
00:47:18,857 --> 00:47:22,235
Seeing how at ease I was and how much fun
I had in front of the camera,

649
00:47:22,319 --> 00:47:24,321
I think I really liked this too.

650
00:47:25,113 --> 00:47:27,950
Did I use any social media by any chance?

651
00:47:29,701 --> 00:47:33,538
If I liked taking pictures so much,
I might have posted them somewhere.

652
00:47:33,622 --> 00:47:38,043
I've already searched for Go Eun-sae
on all the social media platforms,

653
00:47:38,126 --> 00:47:39,795
but I haven't found my account yet.

654
00:47:41,213 --> 00:47:42,923
I'm not sure. I don't think you did.

655
00:47:45,008 --> 00:47:46,385
What about my usual username?

656
00:47:48,220 --> 00:47:49,054
I don't know.

657
00:47:50,347 --> 00:47:53,266
See? This is the kind of thing
that makes me distrust you.

658
00:47:53,350 --> 00:47:55,894
How could you not know
your girlfriend's usual username?

659
00:47:59,523 --> 00:48:03,068
Even if you really are my boyfriend,
I'm disappointed.

660
00:48:03,777 --> 00:48:05,487
Why'd I date such an indifferent guy?

661
00:48:14,329 --> 00:48:18,375
We tried a lot of things,
but I still couldn't remember anything.

662
00:48:18,458 --> 00:48:19,918
It was totally unproductive.

663
00:48:22,879 --> 00:48:24,631
Speaking of productivity,

664
00:48:25,549 --> 00:48:27,384
why do you keep following me around?

665
00:48:27,467 --> 00:48:29,302
Aren't you going to the gym to work?

666
00:48:29,845 --> 00:48:32,889
This is a special situation,
so Mr. Hong understands.

667
00:48:32,973 --> 00:48:34,349
No way.

668
00:48:34,433 --> 00:48:37,894
You must be crazy!

669
00:48:38,395 --> 00:48:41,898
If you just hang around like this at home,
who's going to pay the bills?

670
00:48:41,982 --> 00:48:44,651
I can't exactly go out and work right now.

671
00:48:45,360 --> 00:48:47,446
How are you going to support me?

672
00:48:48,864 --> 00:48:50,949
Ask all the village ladies and see

673
00:48:51,033 --> 00:48:53,952
if any woman would be okay
with her perfectly healthy husband

674
00:48:54,036 --> 00:48:55,245
sitting around at home.

675
00:48:55,829 --> 00:48:56,663
I thought--

676
00:48:56,747 --> 00:48:59,916
There's nothing more for me
to be curious about or find unfamiliar

677
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:02,169
in this tiny village.

678
00:49:02,961 --> 00:49:03,920
So go out

679
00:49:04,421 --> 00:49:05,255
and work.

680
00:49:07,090 --> 00:49:10,302
Men look their best when they're working.

681
00:49:13,138 --> 00:49:16,224
Later, I'm going to help Pil-seung
for a bit with his sparring.

682
00:49:16,308 --> 00:49:17,934
I won't let you go hungry.

683
00:49:18,018 --> 00:49:19,728
Were you even listening?

684
00:49:19,811 --> 00:49:22,606
You're going to go out for a bit
and then come back home?

685
00:49:24,900 --> 00:49:26,026
I'm so sick of this.

686
00:49:26,109 --> 00:49:27,736
Completely sick of this.

687
00:49:28,862 --> 00:49:30,572
How will we afford our beef?

688
00:49:32,240 --> 00:49:34,326
I want to eat beef.

689
00:49:40,415 --> 00:49:41,666
I'd better go make money.

690
00:49:54,262 --> 00:49:56,807
We heard about your date today.

691
00:49:57,390 --> 00:50:00,477
-What?
-The whole village knows.

692
00:50:00,560 --> 00:50:03,647
That the two of you were like a scene
from a romantic movie.

693
00:50:05,023 --> 00:50:08,819
We just rode a scooter for a bit
to see if it would jog her memory.

694
00:50:09,319 --> 00:50:11,863
-And we took some pictures.
-Right.

695
00:50:11,947 --> 00:50:14,825
We were thirsty,
so we bought some drinks. That's all.

696
00:50:14,908 --> 00:50:17,702
That's what we call a date, buddy.

697
00:50:19,454 --> 00:50:22,040
I heard you were lying flat on the ground

698
00:50:22,958 --> 00:50:24,584
just to take her picture!

699
00:50:26,586 --> 00:50:29,422
She kept saying they looked weird
and made me retake them.

700
00:50:30,090 --> 00:50:34,553
They all looked good and pretty to me.
She looked pretty no matter the shot.

701
00:50:36,346 --> 00:50:40,767
Even the pictures she deleted,
saying they looked bad, were pretty.

702
00:50:42,477 --> 00:50:43,478
She kept denying it.

703
00:50:49,151 --> 00:50:50,360
Tae-ha.

704
00:50:51,111 --> 00:50:51,945
Yes, sir?

705
00:50:53,613 --> 00:50:55,115
Sorry about everything.

706
00:50:56,616 --> 00:50:57,617
What?

707
00:50:58,618 --> 00:51:01,621
So this is what it feels like
to have a mirror held up to you.

708
00:51:09,212 --> 00:51:13,592
Why are you going to a PC café
three days in a row?

709
00:51:13,675 --> 00:51:14,509
He's adorable.

710
00:51:14,593 --> 00:51:18,013
What's going to become of you
if you keep playing computer games?

711
00:51:18,096 --> 00:51:19,764
Hey, Geum-hyang.

712
00:51:19,848 --> 00:51:23,810
The idea that video games ruin your life
is old news.

713
00:51:23,894 --> 00:51:26,855
These days, you can earn millions
playing computer games.

714
00:51:27,355 --> 00:51:30,525
If he's not good at studying,
it might be better to get into gaming.

715
00:51:31,818 --> 00:51:35,197
I'm fully supporting
Pil-seung's gaming career.

716
00:51:35,280 --> 00:51:37,741
You even have to support him?

717
00:51:37,824 --> 00:51:39,576
He's already given up on studying.

718
00:51:39,659 --> 00:51:42,746
It's admirable that he's working so hard
on something.

719
00:51:43,455 --> 00:51:45,665
As expected,
you're so open-minded, Hui-ja.

720
00:51:48,084 --> 00:51:52,797
My darling Jun-sik,
cute like the meaty part of a mackerel.

721
00:51:52,881 --> 00:51:54,257
Don't bother.

722
00:51:54,341 --> 00:51:56,218
This 10,000 won is for you.

723
00:51:56,301 --> 00:51:57,302
Thank you.

724
00:51:57,385 --> 00:52:00,180
And Pil-seung is at the PC café, right?

725
00:52:00,263 --> 00:52:03,266
Take this 10,000-won note to Pil-seung.

726
00:52:03,350 --> 00:52:05,018
Pil-seung isn't there.

727
00:52:05,101 --> 00:52:06,811
He's not? What do you mean?

728
00:52:07,479 --> 00:52:10,982
He always goes to the PC café after school
to play computer games.

729
00:52:11,066 --> 00:52:11,900
No, he doesn't.

730
00:52:11,983 --> 00:52:15,612
He wasn't there yesterday
or the day before.

731
00:52:18,240 --> 00:52:22,953
Then where does he go?

732
00:52:23,036 --> 00:52:23,995
Is anything fun on?

733
00:52:24,079 --> 00:52:27,040
…the ceremony for the Irang-dong
development project

734
00:52:27,123 --> 00:52:31,253
was attended by Gangju City officials
and Mirae Eden Company representatives…

735
00:52:31,336 --> 00:52:33,296
They both look so shady.

736
00:52:33,380 --> 00:52:36,049
Their faces really rub me the wrong way.

737
00:52:39,302 --> 00:52:40,512
TOP 3 OMAKASE RESTAURANTS IN SEOUL

738
00:52:40,595 --> 00:52:41,805
Goodness.

739
00:52:42,889 --> 00:52:46,142
What is that? It looks delicious.

740
00:52:46,643 --> 00:52:47,894
Wow.

741
00:52:47,978 --> 00:52:51,564
Look at how shiny the tuna is.
It's totally my thing.

742
00:52:52,065 --> 00:52:54,526
It'd be perfect
if I could eat there right now.

743
00:52:58,113 --> 00:53:00,240
The Cheongdam

744
00:53:01,449 --> 00:53:02,826
Class.

745
00:53:09,457 --> 00:53:11,251
The vibe is amazing.

746
00:53:11,334 --> 00:53:14,587
The people who get to eat here
are so lucky.

747
00:53:14,671 --> 00:53:17,048
I bet it'd be a great spot for photos.

748
00:53:28,768 --> 00:53:29,686
This is

749
00:53:30,353 --> 00:53:31,354
me.

750
00:53:37,485 --> 00:53:38,611
Bestie?

751
00:53:38,695 --> 00:53:39,988
A FEAST WITH MY BESTIE

752
00:53:40,071 --> 00:53:41,072
My friend?

753
00:53:45,201 --> 00:53:49,122
GO JI-WON, PARK HYO-JIN
FOUND A MEMORY WITH JI-WON

754
00:53:56,254 --> 00:53:57,547
It's me.

755
00:53:57,630 --> 00:53:59,341
Yes, this is me.

756
00:54:01,134 --> 00:54:02,177
It's me.

757
00:54:10,685 --> 00:54:14,314
But why does it say "Go Ji-won"
under my photo?

758
00:54:16,524 --> 00:54:19,819
Is my name… Go ji-won?

759
00:54:22,072 --> 00:54:23,114
Go Eun-sae.

760
00:55:34,018 --> 00:55:35,061
They're not here.

761
00:55:35,854 --> 00:55:37,188
They aren't here.

762
00:55:38,189 --> 00:55:41,818
The clothes, this bag, the ring.
Everything in these photos…

763
00:55:44,028 --> 00:55:45,697
None of it's here.

764
00:55:50,493 --> 00:55:52,454
You hated superficial things.

765
00:56:05,925 --> 00:56:06,926
It wasn't true.

766
00:56:08,303 --> 00:56:09,554
None of it was true.

767
00:56:53,806 --> 00:56:56,684
HONG'S BOXING GYM

768
00:57:04,817 --> 00:57:07,529
I can't believe you, Tae-ha. And Mr. Hong!

769
00:57:07,612 --> 00:57:10,698
As adults, how could you just
watch a kid lie and do nothing?

770
00:57:10,782 --> 00:57:13,409
Pil-seung really loves boxing.
And he's good at it.

771
00:57:13,493 --> 00:57:17,205
Save it! So what if he's good?
He'll just end up like you, a thug.

772
00:57:17,997 --> 00:57:20,458
You showed us that yourself.

773
00:57:20,542 --> 00:57:23,878
You even made the national team,
